title: 'M1.6 slice 2 reading: F4 status.cards scoping by class'
summary: 'F4 lists ''inbox by kind'' in status. Reading: the inbox belongs to the human, the only class that decides, so the human gets pendingForYou and byKind; every other class (agent, session, mod, voice, readToken, peer) gets counts only {n, pendingForYou: 0, held}. What is being asked of the human, by kind, is not an agent''s to see. status-numbers already declared cards.byKind.* as optional parts of cards.n, so no clientApiId move.'
